9. ROUND-2 DEVIATIONS WORTH A REVIEWER'S EYE
--------------------------------------------

  - T5 does not carry delta > 0. It follows from 1 <= lam^W * delta, which is
    also assumed, so stating it would state more than is used (SCRUPLES).
    Likewise W = ceil(log_lam(1/delta)) is replaced by the equivalent,
    logarithm-free 1 <= lam^W * delta, which is what T6 and T7 supply.

  - "throughout the run" is formalised as a condition on every prefix of the
    run word: run lam u is the configuration after the first |u| moves.

  - The pigeonhole of T5 is carried out as an induction on the window word
    (card_le_length_succ) rather than as an explicit injection from consecutive
    pairs to moves. The two are the same argument: at a move with a straddling
    pair, deleting the largest knot below the deleted interval both restores the
    gap hypothesis for the image and drops the count by one, which is exactly
    "this move services this pair, and no other".

  - T7's finite verifications are closed by `decide`, i.e. by kernel reduction,
    which the commission permits; `native_decide` is not used anywhere. The
    orbit is stored as integer coordinate triples over Z[rho] and every
    comparison is an integer inequality obtained from the certified enclosure
    1324717957/10^9 <= rho <= 1324717958/10^9. See AXIOM-AUDIT-round2.md, 3.

  - T7 certifies that every reachable knot position is on the 153-point list.
    It does not certify that the list is minimal (that all 153 are attained),
